{"id": 1926379, "name": "C. L. PACE & CO. v. ATLANTIC COAST LINE R. R. CO.", "name_abbreviation": "C. L. Pace & Co. v. Atlantic Coast Line R. R.", "decision_date": "1909-06-09", "docket_number": "7211", "first_page": "33", "last_page": "33", "citations": [{"type": "official", "cite": "83 S.C. 33"}], "court": {"name_abbreviation": "S.C.", "id": 8894, "name": "Supreme Court of South Carolina"}, "jurisdiction": {"id": 59, "name_long": "South Carolina", "name": "S.C."}, "cites_to": [{"cite": "78 S'. C., 81", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [1917261], "opinion_index": -1, "case_paths": ["/sc/78/0081-01"]}, {"cite": "78 S. C., 42", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [1917217], "opinion_index": -1, "case_paths": ["/sc/78/0042-01"]}, {"cite": "66 S. C., 477", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [4417921], "opinion_index": -1, "case_paths": ["/sc/66/0477-01"]}, {"cite": "57 S. E., 1104", "category": "reporters:state_regional", "reporter": "S.E.", "opinion_index": 0}, {"cite": "77 S. C., 319", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [1915510], "opinion_index": 0, "case_paths": ["/sc/77/0319-01"]}], "analysis": {"cardinality": 151, "char_count": 1537, "ocr_confidence": 0.645, "pagerank": {"raw": 2.762287802876944e-07, "percentile": 0.8336663643324379}, "sha256": "7e0ec7ecdb1353f684c2e23afd5423eae219c5d218513b9cd6be38f927474b7d", "simhash": "1:5df91a368c44b453", "word_count": 268}, "last_updated": "2024-02-27T17:26:52.976801+00:00", "provenance": {"date_added": "2019-08-29", "source": "Harvard", "batch": "2018"}, "casebody": {"judges": [], "parties": ["C. L. PACE & CO. v. ATLANTIC COAST LINE R. R. CO."], "opinions": [{"text": "The opinion of the Court was delivered by\nMr. Justice Gary.\nThis is an action for damages to a china closet, and for fifty ($50.00). dollars penalty.\nThe case was tried before a magistrate, who (a jury trial being waived) rendered judgment for the amount claimed and costs, to wit, sixty-six dollars ($66.00i). The defendant appealed to the Circuit Court.\nOn hearing the appeal his Honor, the Circuit Judge, ordered that the judgment of the magistrate be reversed and that a new trial be granted, on the ground that there was no testimony that the goods alleged to have been damaged were injured while in the possession of the defendant. The plaintiff has appealed from said order.\nThe case of Lampley v. Railway Co., 77 S. C., 319, 57 S. E., 1104; shows that said order is not appealable.\nThe order does not determine any of the rights of the parties.\nIt is the judgment of this Court that the appeal herein be dismissed.", "type": "majority", "author": "Mr. Justice Gary."}], "attorneys": ["Mr. James W. Johnson, for appellant.", "Messrs. Montgomery & Lide, contra,"], "corrections": "", "head_matter": "7211\nC. L. PACE & CO. v. ATLANTIC COAST LINE R. R. CO.\nAhpeai,. \u2014 An order reversing judgment of magistrate and ordering new trial because of error of finding of fact is not appealable.\nBefore Shipp, J., Marion, September, 1908.\nAffirmed.\nAction by C. L. Pace & Co. against Atlantic Coast Line Railroad Company. From Circuit order reversing judgment of Magistrate D. J. Oliver, plaintiff appeals.\nMr. James W. Johnson, for appellant.\nOral argument.\nMessrs. Montgomery & Lide, contra,\ncite: Plaintiff did not make out his case: 66 S. C., 477; 78 S. C., 42; Moore on Carriers, 391, 490; 78 S'. C., 81.\nJune 9, 1909."}, "file_name": "0033-01", "first_page_order": 47, "last_page_order": 47}